course: dictionary
lesson: 542
title: Atmosphere: gas and mood
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word atmosphere has two main meanings. The first is the layer of gases, mostly air, that wraps around the Earth or another planet. «Venus's thick atmosphere (its blanket of gas) traps heat.» The words in brackets give you the meaning: a blanket of gas.
explain: The second meaning is the mood or feeling of a place or event. «The Moon has almost no atmosphere, so there is no sound, no wind and the sky is black even in daytime.» Here the word means the gas layer, because the sentence talks about sound, wind and the sky.
explain: Context tells you which meaning you need. Ask: is the sentence about gas around a planet, or about a feeling? Then swap in "layer of air" or "mood" and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: The atmosphere is the layer of gases around the Earth or another planet.
fact: Earth's atmosphere is mostly nitrogen and oxygen.
fact: Earth's atmosphere protects us from the Sun's harmful rays and burns up small meteors.
fact: «Mercury» has almost no atmosphere, so at night its surface falls to about minus 180 degrees Celsius.
fact: The atmosphere of a place can also mean its mood, as in «a friendly atmosphere».
exercise: «Mercury's daytime surface reaches about 430 degrees Celsius, but at night it falls to about minus 180, because it has almost no atmosphere to keep heat in.» What does the atmosphere do here? | *It keeps heat in | It stops the Sun from rising | It makes the planet shine brightly | It makes the planet louder
exercise: «Almost all weather happens in the lowest layer of the atmosphere, the troposphere.» Find and copy the word that names the lowest layer. | almost | *troposphere | lowest | weather
exercise: «The room had a smoky atmosphere.» What does atmosphere mean in this sentence? | A layer of gas around a planet | A loud noise | A type of weather | *The air in the room, which here is smoky
test: Venus, not Mercury, is the hottest planet, because «Venus's thick atmosphere traps heat.» What does traps heat mean? | Lets all the heat escape quickly | Makes the planet cold | *Keeps heat in, like a blanket | Makes the planet move closer to the Sun
test: A writer wants a scary atmosphere in a story. Which words would help build that feeling? | sunny, warm, busy | happy, loud, bouncy | cold, fast, shiny | *dark, silent, creaking
exam: Which sentence uses atmosphere to mean the layer of gases around a planet? | «The classroom had a friendly atmosphere.» | *«Earth's atmosphere protects us from the Sun's harmful rays.» | «The party had a happy atmosphere.» | «The smoky atmosphere made her cough.»
